  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nToday through Saturday: High and mid level clouds continue to \nstream across the CWA through today, with mainly dry and quiet \nweather expected into tonight. Gusty west winds will persist into \nthe afternoon. A Lake Wind Advisory runs till 5PM Friday with wave\nheights as high as 5 feet at times. A cold front will arrive \ntonight brining additional gusty winds on Saturday. In addition \nmost CAMs are siting a system of light rain/snow showers moving NW\nto SE across the northeastern half of the CWA. The QPF with these\nshowers should not amount to much at all through with light \nsprinkles or flurries possible depending on the timing of the \npassage. CAMs do vary in the 6 hour passage timing of these \nshowers.\n\nSaturday through Sunday: expect zonal to northwest flow and dry\nconditions with near normal temps. \n\nMonday into Tuesday: with the breakdown of a weak ridge a slightly\nSW tilt will enter the zonal flow. Ensemble runs are going back\nand forth as to whether to include scattered light snow showers\nwith the entrance of this feature from forecast to forecast.\nRegardless,m QPF won't be much of anything here. \n\nTuesday night onward: Flow returns to zonal with dry conditions \nand near normal temps for highs and above normal temps for low. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\nDeviations from NBM include... NBM PoPs were ignoring (0%) \nrain/snow showers across the northeast Saturday morning around 9AM\nthrough Midnight. Had to go in an used a blend of HRRR, RRFS, and\nCMCreg CAMs to try to bring this feature back into the forecast \nfor these time periods. \n\nConfidence is HIGH through Sunday night.\n\nConfidence is MODERATE from Monday onward.\n\nGAH",
